<title>AUSTRIA: Austrian Airlines wins approval for Lauda deal.</title>
<headline>Austrian Airlines wins approval for Lauda deal.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Airlines has won cartel authority clearance to buy a 35.9 percent voting stake in former rival Lauda Air, chief executive Mario Rehulka told a shareholders meeting on Monday.</p>
<p>Austria's flag carrier announced in March it had acquired the shares along with an option to buy founder Niki Lauda's remaining 30 percent holding at a fixed price by 2022.</p>
<p>At the same time Germany's Lufthansa cut its Lauda stake to 20 percent from 39.7 percent.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
